thod":"IP/resistivity","page":17,"text":"In the 1980s, Agnico Eagle completed a shallow IP survey which yielded several chargeability anomalies."},{"method":"magnetics","page":17,"text":"its work on base metal exploration, carried out drilling on coincident ground magnetic and electromagnetic (EM) anomalies. From 1966 to 1970, Equity Exploration\u2019s successor Eagle Gold Mines Ltd.","platform":"ground","year":1959},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":17,"text":"From 1966 to 1970, Equity Exploration\u2019s successor Eagle Gold Mines Ltd.","year":1966},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":19,"text":"geophysical surveys, including three ground IP, airborne magnetic and EM surveys, as well as an Artificial Intelligence (AI) study using all available data generated in the central part of the Project, covering a 17 km segme","platform":"airborne","year":2020},{"method":"borehole geophysics","page":19,"text":"Subsequent borehole EM surveys conducted in 2022\u2013 2023 at the Eagle and Telbel areas refined the understanding of sulphide-hosted conductive horizons and confirmed b","platform":"borehole","year":2024},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":36,"text":"Subsequent detailed ground magnetic and induced polarization (IP) surveys were used to identify targets that were drilled and identified as Z10, 531 Zone (in 1986), and Douay West (DW) Zone (in","platform":"ground","year":1976},{"method":"magnetics","page":36,"text":"work on the search for base metals and carried out drilling on coincident ground magnetic (Mag) and electromagnetic (EM) anomalies. 1966-1971 In 1966, Eagle Gold Mines Ltd.","platform":"ground","year":1966},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":36,"text":"1966-1971 In 1966, Eagle Gold Mines Ltd. acquired Equity Exploration and carried out underground development on a gold-bea","platform":"ground","year":1966},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":38,"text":"In the 1980s, Agnico Eagle completed a shallow IP survey which yielded several chargeability anomalies.","year":1978},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":72,"text":"2011 IP and Resistivity/IP survey on the northern half of the Porphyry Zone and the DW, Nika, and NW zones (60 line-km) Successfully delineated some of the known zone","year":2011,"line_km":60.0,"line_spacing_m":100.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":72,"text":"Year Activity Remarks Geophysical Surveys 2011 High resolution helicopter magnetic survey 1,968 line-km on 100 m grid at 25 m above surface producing three maps on a scale of 1:25,000 A prominent, highly magnetic structure that","year":2011,"line_km":1968.0},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":73,"text":"2021 IP Survey 49.8 line-km of IP & 15 line-km of IP Two grids to compare the sediment hosted gold chargeability against the basalt/syenite hosted gold chargea","year":2021,"platform":"airborne","line_km":49.8},{"method":"magnetics","page":73,"text":"2026 Aeromagnetic and FALCON\u00ae Airborne Gravity Gradiometer 2,506-line-km Larger survey covering western portion of the Douay property.","platform":"airborne","year":2025,"line_km":841.0},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":73,"text":"Signal much clearer in basalt/syenite. 2021-2022 Mag/EM Airborne (VTEM) 2,029 line-km Property scale versatile time-domain EM (VTEM) survey on western side of property (including Joutel).","platform":"airborne","year":2021,"line_km":2029.0},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":76,"text":"In 2011, Abitibi Geophysics Inc. (Abitibi Geophysics) completed a resistivity/IP survey, using the IPOWER 3D system, covering the northern half of the Porphyry Zone and the DW, Nika, and NW zones.","year":2011,"platform":"ground","line_km":11.0,"line_spacing_m":100.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":76,"text":"(Novatem) was contracted by Vior, in partnership with Maple Gold, to complete a high-resolution helicopter magnetic","year":2026},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":77,"text":"24, 2026 SLR Project No.: 233.065515.00001 9-6 Results showed moderate resistivities (100 \u03a9m to 4,500 \u03a9m), reflecting 10 m to 15 m (locally thicker) of in part conductive overburden, with thinner overburden in the central por","year":2026,"platform":"ground","line_km":5.7,"line_spacing_m":400.0},{"method":"magnetics","page":77,"text":"2020 Airborne Magnetic Survey In late 2020, Maple Gold commissioned Prospectair Inc. to carry out an airborne magnetic survey consisting of 841 line-km in the eastern p","platform":"airborne","year":2020,"line_km":841.0},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":78,"text":"For the NW Grid, resistivities ranged from 4 \u03a9m to 54,587 \u03a9m, with chargeability values of up to 36.3 mV/V.","year":2026,"platform":"airborne"},{"method":"magnetics","page":78,"text":"2024 Airborne Magnetic Survey A 525.2-line-km drone magnetic survey was flown between May 25 and May 30, 2024, over the far western portion of Douay property by Vision4","platform":"airborne","year":2024,"line_km":525.2},{"method":"gravity","page":78,"text":"2026 Airborne Gravity Survey A 2,506-line-km high-sensitivity aeromagnetic and FALCON\u00ae Airborne Gravity Gradiometer (AGG) survey was flown between March 4 and March 13,","platform":"airborne","year":2026,"line_km":2506.0},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":81,"text":"Additionally, comparisons were made with anomalous Cu, Zn values. The report provides assurance that expenditures will be allocated to claims a","year":2022},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":83,"text":"drive exploration results 9.2.3 Geophysical Surveys 2022-2023 Borehole EM Surveys Maple Gold commissioned a series of borehole EM surveys conducted by TMC on the Eagle and Telbel claims in 2022 and 2023.","platform":"borehole","year":2022},{"method":"borehole geophysics","page":83,"text":"and drive exploration results 9.2.3 Geophysical Surveys 2022-2023 Borehole EM Surveys Maple Gold commissioned a series of borehole EM surveys conducted by TMC on the Eagle and Telbel claims in 2022 and 2023.","platform":"borehole","year":2022},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":97,"text":"8 Regional Exploration: discovery of JDZE by testing chargeability anomaly. Key results from the 2021-2022 drilling include: \u2022 531 Zone \u2013 Hole DO-21-316 intersected 1.5 g/t Au over 32.2 m (from 430.0 m downh","year":2021},{"method":"IP/resistivity","page":196,"text":"geophysical surveys (magnetic, horizontal loop electromagnetic (HLEM), resistivity, and IP surveys) and drilled 36 holes totalling 10,209 m. In early 1987, Radisson completed additional IP and magnetic surveys.","year":1984},{"method":"magnetics","page":196,"text":"In early 1987, Radisson completed additional IP and magnetic surveys. Drilling identified two major fault zones, which form part of the broader CBDZ.","year":1987},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":196,"text":"has conducted ground geophysical surveys (magnetic, horizontal loop electromagnetic (HLEM), resistivity, and IP surveys) and drilled 36 holes totalling 10,209 m.","platform":"ground","year":1984},{"method":"magnetics","page":203,"text":"of Western Ontario M.Sc. thesis, 160p Boivin, M. 2024. Report on a drone magnetic survey over the Joutel West Project. Montgolfier and Valrennes Townships. NTS 32E/09 and 32E/10. Qu\u00e9bec, Canada, 12p. Bouchard, M. 2017.","year":1979},{"method":"electromagnetics","page":203,"text":"Geotech Ltd. 2022. Report on a Helicopter-Borne Versatile Time Domain Electromagnetic (VTEMTM Plus) and Horizontal Magnetic Gradiometer Geophysical Survey, 27 p. Geostat, Systemes Geostat Internation Inc. 2005.","platform":"airborne","year":2022}],"targets":[{"page":17,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"From 1966 to 1970, Equity Exploration\u2019s successor Eagle Gold Mines Ltd. (Eagle) carried out development on an auriferous pyrite deposit, with underground mining development initiated in 1967 and continued until 1970."},{"page":36,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"1966-1971 In 1966, Eagle Gold Mines Ltd. acquired Equity Exploration and carried out underground development on a gold-bearing pyrite deposit which became the Eagle Mine."},{"page":38,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"In the 1980s, Agnico Eagle completed a shallow IP survey which yielded several chargeability anomalies. These were, however, interpreted to reflect variations in overburden thickness rather than the presence of disseminated sulphide."},{"page":76,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"The survey showed that the Douay deposits are associated with a distinctive \u201cmottled\u201d pattern, which includes both magnetic highs (mostly metasomatized basalts) and depressions (typically syenitic rocks), both of which can host gold mineralization."},{"page":77,"explained":true,"untested":false,"text":"At the SW Grid, similar resistivities were obtained (22 \u03a9m to 3,781 \u03a9m) but significantly higher chargeability (up to 18.9 mV/V, average 5.1 mV/V). The SW Grid chargeability anomaly coincides with and extends beyond known mineralization of the 531 Zone."}]},"rock":{"density":{"n":12,"min":2.72,"max":2.85,"median":2.85,"page":11,"text":"For all other zones, bulk density ranging between 2.72 t/m\u00b3 and 2.88 t/m\u00b3 was assigned to Mineral Resources based on the zone."},"overburden_m":{"n":2,"min":50.0,"max":100.0,"median":100.0,"page":76,"text":"Although the overburden thickness is more than 50 m over much of this grid, the IPOWER 3D survey successfully delineated some of the known zones of mineralization."},"density_samples":{"n":1,"min":2.0,"max":2.0,"median":2.0,"page":89,"text":"10.2.11 Specific Gravity Samples of whole core, and occasionally half core, usually ranging from 5 cm to 50 cm, were collected every 6 m."}},"model_params":{"density":2.85,"default_cutoff":0.98,"method":"idw","power":3.0,"metallurgy":{"routes":["flotation","gravity"],"traits":["transitional","sulphide","arsenic"],"recoveries":null,"summary":"transitional ore present, sulphide ore, arsenic-bearing; processed by flotation to concentrate, then gravity recovery"},"deposit_style":"vms"},"effec